Theorem 5. Rules 200 and 204 always reach fixed points.
Proof. Rule 204 is the identity rule, meaning that all configurations are fixed
points, and the only difference between rules 200 and 204 is f204 (010) =
1 ̸= 0 = f200 (010), which means that for rule 204 all configurations are
fixed points except for the ones that have isolated 1’s, because said 1’s will
disappear as soon as the cell in which they are located is updated.

