t = 2 the 1 advances again, but since the next cell to the right is updated
before the one on the right, we gain ones until the first cell such that µi >
µi+1 , which means that it is a cell in {ri }ji=1 . Let us call that cell r1 .
t = 3 We continue to gain ones until the next cell to the right that belongs
to {ri }ji=1 , which will be r2 . In this instance, we do not lose ones to the left,
because f1 84(001) = 0 and f184 (011) = 1.
